## Import

Import uses `workspace_id/team_id`, with two native IDs separated by a slash. Neither ID may contain a slash.

{{ codefile "shell" .ImportFile }}

Find IDs with the authenticated `/api/auth/organization/list-teams?organizationId=workspace-id` endpoint. Names are not unique identifiers.

Kaneo 2.23.2 seeds a default team named after the workspace and adds the workspace creator to it. Import that team to manage it; creation always adds another team, even when the name matches. Kaneo limits each workspace to 10 teams, including the default team.

## Deletion and recovery

Kaneo prohibits deleting the last team. Terraform retains state and reports an error. Keep an unmanaged default team, or create another team before retrying deletion. Managing every team can block a full Terraform destroy because dependent teams are deleted before their workspace. To delete the workspace out of band instead, refresh afterward to reconcile state.

Better Auth also rejects deleting the session's active team. Clear the active team for that session before retrying; the provider does not change session selection. Team deletion removes its memberships and strips its ID from pending invitations.

Refresh validates every returned team's identity and workspace, rejects duplicate IDs, and only then checks absence. The list endpoint has no pagination and Better Auth caps it at 100 rows. Kaneo's 10-team limit stays below that cap; the provider fails closed if a response reaches 100. Custom server limits or filtering can invalidate this assumption.

A complete scoped list can prove team absence. Only an explicit not-found response from the workspace presence endpoint proves parent absence. Lost access, authentication failures, malformed responses, and generic 404s retain state. Restore access before retrying. If creation succeeds remotely but its response is lost or invalid, inspect the team list and import the created ID before applying again.
